96","fullName":"Rep. Boyle, Brendan F. [D-PA-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"},{"bioguideId":"C001080","fullName":"Rep. Chu, Judy [D-CA-28]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"S001223","fullName":"Rep. Sykes, Emilia Strong [D-OH-13]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OH"},{"bioguideId":"P000620","fullName":"Rep. Pettersen, Brittany [D-CO-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CO"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T22:54:26+00:00","id":"hr5619-119","introducedDate":"2025-09-30","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-09-30","text":"Referred to the Committee on Appropriations, and in addition to the Committee on Oversight and Government Reform, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"laws":[],"number":"5619","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Economics and Public Finance","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"B001326","district":5,"fullName":"Rep. Bynum, Janelle S. [D-OR-5]","party":"D","state":"OR"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-09-30","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Federal Firefighter Paycheck Protection Act</strong></p><p>This bill provides continuing FY2026 appropriations to pay federal firefighters if a government shutdown is in effect. It also prohibits the firefighters from being subject to a reduction in force (RIF) during a government shutdown.&nbsp;</p><p>Specifically, the bill provides continuing FY2026 appropriations to provide pay and allowances to federal firefighters during any period in which interim or full-year appropriations for FY2026 are not in effect (i.e., a government shutdown). The bill provides the appropriations until the earlier of (1) the enactment of specified appropriations legislation, or (2) January 1, 2027.</p><p>The bill also prohibits federal firefighters from being removed from the civil service due to a RIF during a government shutdown.&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-10-01T17:39:00Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Federal Firefighter Paycheck Protection Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2025-11-01T08:05:29Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2025-11-01T08:05:29Z"}
